//// log — levels and per-name thresholds, the log record, the four
//// renderers, the one error digest, a `Logger` whose sink is injected, the
//// console, file and fan-out sinks, and the capture of the runtime's own
//// reports. A library (decisions 194, 195, 349), neutral like `routing`: it
//// imports `std` and nothing else, ships `.bp` files only (decision 117 rule
//// 8) and is compiled from one source for every target, so a line and a
//// digest read the same everywhere.
////
//// Consumers write `import {logging.Logger, digest.errorDigest} from "log";`
//// (decision 107). Moved from rakun-logging's pure half (`levels.bp`,
//// `formats.bp`, `digest.bp`, the `Logger`); its sinks and its capture are
//// `log`'s (349) — rakun and onze choose, configure and install one at boot.
//// See `../AGENTS.md`.
////
//// The `files` ORDER in `botopink.json` is a dependency order: a module is
//// listed before the siblings that import it.

pub mod levels;
pub mod formats;
pub mod digest;
pub mod sink;
pub mod logfile;
pub mod logging;
pub mod reports;
